# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Linux CI job only (macOS needs none).
# Each entry names a report that is known not to be a data race. Keep the list
# short; never add an entry without the reason.

# SQLite: unixOpen resets the PRNG when the process ID changes. SQLite's own
# comment at that line documents the race between threads opening databases at
# the same instant as harmless (it can only reseed more than once).
race:unixOpen

# Swift's Synchronization.Mutex locks on Linux with futex system calls inside the
# precompiled, uninstrumented standard library, so ThreadSanitizer cannot see the
# lock and reports the protected accesses as races. Every reported access in these
# types happens inside `withLock`. macOS ThreadSanitizer, which does see the lock
# (os_unfair_lock), checks the same Swift code without suppressions.
race:SlotPool
